quiet.md: KeyBinding::load_unmapped

Upstream's KeyBinding::load takes an &App and maps keystrokes through the
platform keyboard mapper, which on Windows rewrites them even without key
equivalents. The app builds its Windows and Linux bindings, and the user's
own shortcuts, from strings at startup and wants them parsed as written, as
GPUI 0.2's load with a DummyKeyboardMapper did: add load_unmapped(keys,
action, predicate, action_input, os).

